    "q-112097": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112097",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242840/assets/2bf74d1a67facef247993de2849d94918a0492acdf69b9086ac1e48a913bc6f2.png)\n\nWhich of the following polynomials could be the function shown in the diagram above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's call $P(x)$ the polynomial shown in the diagram.\n\nThe end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is positive.\n\n- the $y$-intercept is $0,$ which means that $P(0)=0.$\n\nTherefore, of the given options, the only one that satisfies all three criteria is $y=3{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-4x.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
