    "q-38581": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38581",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242840/assets/2c62bf5398a58cf3e27b3a47f4494fccc6d89e453685d1cd8620588c3d2bb2fa.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n\nII. $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n\nIII. The degree of $P(x)$ is odd.",
      "worked_solution": "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statement I is false, while statements II and III are true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
