    "q-112114": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112114",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242840/assets/b46093feaf5d7138e30c6d6fc673a2d915cac74a23ae76e0841e9bb5b135fa60.png)\n\nThe graph of the polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The degree of $P(x)$ is even.\n\nII. The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n\nIII. The constant term is positive.",
      "worked_solution": "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nSo, statement I is true, while statement II is false.\n\nLastly, note that the $y$-intercept is positive, and therefore the constant term must be positive. So, III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
