    "q-112109": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112109",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242840/assets/1a91d10c69c8d466b6155f775ebd0856003889089cc41a3246ec0a812b58def3.png)\n\nThe graph of the polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The degree of $P(x)$ is odd.\n\nII. $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIII. The coefficient of the leading term is negative.",
      "worked_solution": "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false.",
